<title>USA: Phillips Petroleum may issue $350 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Phillips Petroleum may issue $350 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum is expected to tap the market with a $350 million debt offering via Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, high-grade syndicate sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to consist of a 40-year trust preferred issue with a call option in the tenth year, sources said.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>((--Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
